= Decentralized identity — Technical =

A DID is a URI identifying a DID subject and resolving, according to a DID method, to a DID document that can contain verification methods and services. Security depends on controller-key management, resolution integrity, credential issuer trust, revocation/status, privacy, and governance.

== Modeling / security cautions ==
* decentralized identity ≠ blockchain identity
* DID ≠ person
* decentralization ≠ absence of issuers, governance, or trust

